# Regression fixture: `tan(theta)` used where a real trigonometric
# tangent was clearly intended. Before RESERVED_FN_NAMES existed, this
# metric would have been silently ACCEPTED -- `tan` parsing as an
# opaque indeterminate function -- and any query differentiating it
# would have produced a plausible-looking but wrong answer (an ordinary
# indeterminate `tan'`, never the real sec^2). Must be a clean parse
# error instead, naming the reservation, never a computed result.
manifold M dim 2
bundle TM on M dim 2
chart c on M coords (r, theta)
metric g on c bundle TM {
  [r,r] = 1,
  [theta,theta] = tan(theta)^2
}
